{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>The young woman shall stay with us.</b> And if you ask: have they not already said, 'Here is Rebekah before you, take and go'? Rather, at first they did not know that he was an emissary to betroth; therefore they said, 'Take and go' — bring her to Isaac that he may betroth her. But afterward, when they saw that he himself had betrothed her, then they said: since she is betrothed, <b>the young woman shall stay with us</b> etc., as we learned: they give a virgin twelve months after her betrothal." "<b>Days or a ten-day period.</b> Days — twelve months, as it is written, 'כדת הנשים שנים עשר חדש' etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:42.577702038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}